  "visual_differences": {
    "all": "The Godot HUD uses its existing typography, dimensions and outlines. Panels use the existing font spacing, corner radii and button widths.",
    "s01_s12_s13": "The native market map has thinner marker and text outlines and a ring around the closed gate marker. The current UI positions the place bar using the text width.",
    "s02_to_s08": "Godot's placeholder street and capsules replace the rendered spice street and stall backdrop. The panel can overlay Rashid's name. The status labels and controls align to the right. The discovery notice wraps across two lines.",
    "s06_s07": "The live clock at Spice row shows Dhuhr on Friday under LOCK 2's away-from-Masjid rule. The masters say Friday prayer.",
    "s09_to_s11": "The bag opens on the live Inn street with placeholder geometry and capsules behind the centered panel.",
    "s10_s11": "The tested wallet and trust are 163 and 23. Both masters show 160 and 20.",
    "s12_s13": "The live wallet is 197 coins. Trust goes from 22 to 23. The masters use 198 coins and 20 to 21 trust. The native toast is narrower with a border and less rounding.",
    "s14_s15": "Reputation uses the live Inn and Spice row viewpoints. The native wallets are 163 and 172. The masters show 198. Trust matches at 23 and 17.",
    "street_capsules": "Two additional frames show the labeled Rashid and Faris placeholder capsules in their respective places."
  },
